<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47458" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠπεδᾰνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>weakly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.104
			</span></i>; <i>halting</i>, of Hephaistos, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.311
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρες, χέρες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.800
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.82
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					<u>Fab.Hex.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					2.160
				</span></i>
			; in 
				Ion.
			 Prose, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. πῦρ</span>
			<i>a slight, trifling</i> fever, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.4
			</span></i>; of a child, <i>weakly</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἠ</span>. ib.<i><span class="en">
				78
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. ὕπνος</span>
			<i>light, slight</i>, dub. in Ion Trag.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; of ghosts, prob. cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				134
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen.,
				<i>void of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάμας ἔσσεαι ἠπεδανά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.521
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>weakening</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>L.</u>
					382
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				142
			</span></i>. (Derived by Gramm. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span>
			priv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέδον</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				433.26
			</span></i>, and 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηπεδανός</span>
			: better fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πούς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; for the termination perh. cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐτιδ-ανός</span>.)</div>
